{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfVsfKdnzGwbUXtHUtcXA", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "```\n\u2717 Playwright MCP is not connected.\n\nunderstudy drives a real browser through the Playwright MCP server. Without it,\ntraversal cannot run.\n\n  claude mcp add playwright npx @playwright/mcp@latest\n\nThen restart Claude Code and run /understudy:run again.\n```\n\nI stopped at pre-flight. I checked two ways: no Playwright tools are loaded in this session, and `claude mcp list` says \"No MCP servers configured.\"\n\nI didn't try to get around this by fetching the pages of https://example-nimbus-notes.test over HTTP and scoring them for clarity and trust. That wouldn't be a real visit, and the report would look like one when it isn't.\n\nOnce Playwright is added and you've restarted Claude Code, run `/understudy:run https://example-nimbus-notes.test`. It starts with a short interview before the browser opens: personas, device, time cap and where the report goes. Your URL and your choice of clarity and trust answer part of it, so it should be quick."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 368, "cache_read_input_tokens": 31509, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 368}, "output_tokens": 329, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "16ce2452-94c4-42a0-a62e-c3e51398f2bd", "uuid": "1f8b7625-5a20-49e6-b01f-7da8144672b5", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T12:56:28.533Z", "request_id": "req_011CfVsfKHSjP6i61xwXSnxi"}
